    "body": "Looks already fixed on upstream/main e902ee488: the failure does not reproduce without a change.\n\nEvidence:\n- Local run on e902ee488 (debug, macOS): `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test example_catalog catalog_3d_rough_finish -- --test-threads=2`. All 7 tests pass.\n- `catalog 3d/rough-finish regenerates elapsed=17.076s budget=60.000s`\n- `catalog 3d/rough-finish rebuilds elapsed=18.915s budget=60.000s`\n\nCause of the red run 45951033939:\n- The two tests failed the 60 s case budget of `run_case` (`within` in `crates/app/tests/example_catalog/support.rs`). The step took 138 s. The log shows no assertion failure.\n- The runner was under load. The same job stopped on the 75-minute \"Batch gate tier\" timeout at 07:34.\n- #4286 (41a4e01eb) changed only the stamps and the project version in `rough-finish.camproj`. The cases need about 18 s locally, so that change does not explain a 138 s step.\n\nThe post-merge run for 62456d0a6 is green, but it skipped the gate (process-only change). The run for e902ee488 (45953797437) is in progress. It is the first run that tests this code again.\n\nThis is a runner stop under \"Runner stops\" (#3303), not a red main. Suggest closing when run 45953797437 is green; the maintainer decides. I release my claim.\n\n<!-- ownership: writer -->\nOwnership released: mkinney / m3 pool job issue-4322\nBranch: mkinney/Camcraft issue/4322-rough-finish-catalog (never pushed)\nState: released\n",
